00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:10.800
Super Cheap

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:13.010
<i>It’s an amazing offer! White radishes are 10 yen each! Only 10 yen!</i>

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:15.000
<i>Grab one while supplies last!</i>

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.830
Onee-chan, leave this to me!

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:21.170
Go ahead, Asu!

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:27.100
Ah, there’s only one left!

00:03:35.050 --> 00:03:37.970
Ah, the last white radish…

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:43.570
Let’s go.

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:44.030
Okay.

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:48.750
The white radishes are all sold out!

00:03:54.770 --> 00:03:56.980
We were just a bit too late.

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:01.550
Ah! Look, look, Onee-chan!

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:03.720
Tomorrow’s special is meat!

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:04.780
Meat?!

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:08.430
You’re right! It really is meat!

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:10.930
Pork Cutlets

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:14.510
100 grams of pork cutlets for only 88 yen!

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:15.900
How long has it been?

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:22.360
Tomorrow, let’s try harder!

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:23.570
Yes!

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:27.360
Meat! Tomorrow we’re having meat!

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:30.820
Meat! Tomorrow we’re having meat!

00:04:39.190 --> 00:04:40.880
Asu-chan, you’re going home already?

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:42.840
Yes!

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:46.070
Today, pork cutlets are on sale for 88 yen.

00:04:47.210 --> 00:04:48.300
See you!

00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:54.770
<i>It’s the girl from yesterday.</i>

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:56.730
<i>It seems she’s from the class next door.</i>

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:05.070
<i>She’s not going to the same supermarket again, is she?</i>

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:06.820
<i>I have to hurry.</i>

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:14.460
Super Cheap

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:14.700
<i>Calm down, there’s still a lot left!</i>

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:17.230
<i>Yes, here you go!</i>

00:05:17.230 --> 00:05:19.000
<i>Pork cutlets for 88 yen!</i>

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:24.920
Ah! There’s only one left!

00:05:29.710 --> 00:05:33.060
Let go! I got here first.

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:34.410
No way…

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:36.080
This is mine!

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:43.510
Meat! Meat! We’re having yummy meat for dinner!

00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:44.290
Meat!

00:05:44.290 --> 00:05:45.220
Meat!

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:46.060
Meat!

00:05:46.060 --> 00:05:47.060
Meat!

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:47.960
Meat!

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:49.320
Meat!

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:50.870
No!

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:55.950
Please…

00:05:58.140 --> 00:06:01.870
If I don’t buy this, my sister will yell at me.

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:07.090
Your sister… you mean that person from yesterday?

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:09.220
Don’t cry.

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:13.630
The meat’s mine.

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:16.340
Oh, please excuse me.

00:06:16.340 --> 00:06:18.400
Thank goodness there was still one left.

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:22.410
The pork cutlets are sold out!

00:06:29.050 --> 00:06:30.870
It’s all sold out!

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:32.510
Why wouldn’t you let me have it?

00:06:33.940 --> 00:06:35.370
<i>Is she faking it again?</i>

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:39.900
Just because you wouldn’t let go…

00:06:43.780 --> 00:06:46.300
<i>No, she’s really crying.</i>

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:54.430
What should I do? If I don’t bring that meat home, my sister will yell at me.

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:57.080
No, she’ll probably kick me out.

00:06:57.080 --> 00:06:59.640
I might not have a home to go back to anymore.

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:02.610
If you tell her what happened, she’ll understand.

00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:06.290
You’re only saying that because you don’t know my sister!

00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:08.420
She’s a strict perfectionist,

00:07:08.420 --> 00:07:09.900
so there’s no way she’ll understand!

00:07:10.710 --> 00:07:13.100
Is she really that strict?

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:21.080
She’s completely different from my sister.

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:22.130
That’s right.

00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:23.300
I know!

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:27.380
It’s your fault I can’t go home, so let me live at your house!

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:29.970
What?

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:32.410
Um, well…

00:07:34.790 --> 00:07:36.420
I’m back.

00:07:37.820 --> 00:07:40.230
Welcome home, Asu!

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:46.860
Aren’t you the girl from yesterday?

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:49.770
You see, Onee-chan, um…

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:53.570
I didn’t get any of the pork cutlets.

00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:56.210
Ah, you don’t have to worry about that.

00:07:56.980 --> 00:07:58.890
Here, see?

00:07:58.890 --> 00:08:01.670
Onee-chan, how did you get this meat?

00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:06.920
I told myself that I’d definitely make it to today’s big sale.

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:09.230
So, right after school, I rushed to the store.

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:14.210
To prevent yesterday’s events from happening again, I was twice as cautious.

00:08:14.410 --> 00:08:16.680
Wow, you’re amazing, Onee-chan! As expected!

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:19.200
Thanks!

00:08:28.670 --> 00:08:29.810
Onee-chan.

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:32.900
I have a request.

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:33.820
What’s wrong?

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:37.330
I want you to give this meat to her.

00:08:39.800 --> 00:08:42.770
Her sister is very strict.

00:08:42.770 --> 00:08:46.650
Without any of the meat from the sale, she can’t go home.

00:08:47.240 --> 00:08:54.220
So, Onee-chan, give her the pork cutlets that you bought.

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:57.180
Please.

00:08:57.480 --> 00:09:00.770
What are you talking about!? Forget about it!

00:09:00.770 --> 00:09:04.690
Besides, there’s no way you’d just give that away to a stranger.{probably should be “those” but fuckit, it looked weird}

00:09:10.030 --> 00:09:11.640
Here, take it.

00:09:12.470 --> 00:09:15.080
How can you just give it away so easily?

00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:17.490
Isn’t this your dinner?

00:09:17.490 --> 00:09:21.440
Well, that’s because Asu asked me to.

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:24.930
Asu seriously wants me to give this to you.

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:27.980
I’m sure she has an important reason for asking.

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:31.110
After all, she wouldn’t ask without a reason.

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:38.440
And you! How can you so easily give away something that your sister worked so hard to buy?

00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:41.160
Weren’t you worried your sister would yell at you?

00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:47.650
Well, Onee-chan only gets angry when I do something that troubles others.

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:51.510
Even without the meat, we can still eat dinner together.

00:09:51.510 --> 00:09:57.660
Even though meat is delicious, as long as I can eat dinner with Asu, anything will taste delicious.

00:09:57.910 --> 00:09:58.700
Right?

00:09:59.030 --> 00:09:59.940
Right?

00:10:13.510 --> 00:10:15.320
It’s completely different in my family.

00:10:16.610 --> 00:10:21.930
They don’t trust me at all, because I’m always making mistakes.{Comma: Gramtically incorrect? Yes. Required for the line to flow with audio? Also yes.}

00:10:25.540 --> 00:10:29.790
I think you need this pork more than we do.

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:34.710
Go make your sister proud of you, okay?

00:10:45.260 --> 00:10:48.060
It’s getting late, let us take you home.

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:49.670
Th-Thank you.

00:10:51.070 --> 00:10:54.010
<i>And that is how our summer ended.</i>

00:10:54.450 --> 00:10:58.800
<i>To this girl, the 100 grams of pork cutlets on sale for 88 yen</i>

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:04.370
<i>were probably important in building a bond of trust between her and her sister.</i>

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:10.770
<i>But why it had to be on sale was something Onee-chan and I didn’t understand.</i>

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:14.510
<i>Because, when she led us to her house…</i>

00:11:16.180 --> 00:11:17.920
My name is Echigoya Ginko.

00:11:18.230 --> 00:11:20.050
This is my house.

00:11:27.400 --> 00:11:29.720
<i>Her house was fit for a king.{王子 【おうじ】 (n) prince}</i>

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:38.130
Keeping an eye out for
even a small discount,
Asu moves at full speed

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:38.130
One for 10 yen

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:46.640
Even the raindrops leaking
from the roof can sound
like a soothing orchestra

00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:51.350
They have a lot of money, right?

00:11:51.350 --> 00:11:52.850
Yeah. This is unbelievable.

00:11:52.850 --> 00:11:55.360
Why does she have to buy food that’s on sale?

00:11:55.800 --> 00:11:57.000
John!

00:12:04.450 --> 00:12:06.060
I wonder why…

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:08.130
It’s dinner time.

00:12:13.880 --> 00:12:15.210
It’s an alligator.

00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:16.540
The pork was food for the alligator…

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:19.880
Ginko.

00:12:26.900 --> 00:12:28.240
Onee-sama!

00:12:29.070 --> 00:12:31.540
I am Echigoya Kinko, the older sister.

00:12:32.470 --> 00:12:33.890
I’m Yamada Kyou.

00:12:33.890 --> 00:12:35.280
I’m Asu.

00:12:35.280 --> 00:12:36.910
Looks like they get along well.

00:12:36.910 --> 00:12:37.670
Yes.

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:41.210
Onee-sama, I managed to buy the big sale item—

00:12:41.210 --> 00:12:42.630
You didn’t buy it, right?

00:12:43.730 --> 00:12:46.830
I was worried about you, so I followed you.

00:12:46.830 --> 00:12:49.210
Why must you lie about it?

00:12:49.210 --> 00:12:52.760
If you didn’t buy it, why didn’t you just honestly say so?

00:12:52.760 --> 00:12:54.090
I’m sorry.

00:12:58.340 --> 00:12:59.840
Ah, um…

00:13:01.230 --> 00:13:04.570
I apologize for the trouble my sister gave you. Good day.

00:13:04.570 --> 00:13:05.560
Ah, yes.

00:13:12.530 --> 00:13:14.220
Will she be okay?

00:13:14.220 --> 00:13:16.020
I’m sure she’ll be fine…

00:13:27.110 --> 00:13:30.670
Tomorrow, at the supermarket in the next town…

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:34.040
1 day sale

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:34.040
3 carrots
for 50 yen

00:13:31.380 --> 00:13:36.000
Carrots are on sale—three for 50 yen.

00:13:44.440 --> 00:13:48.030
I wonder why the Echigoya sisters go bargain hunting.

00:13:48.030 --> 00:13:50.600
It seems pointless since they’re rich.

00:13:50.880 --> 00:13:52.670
I wonder why.

00:13:52.670 --> 00:13:53.530
Ah!

00:13:53.530 --> 00:13:55.330
Look, look, Onee-chan!

00:13:55.330 --> 00:13:57.190
What? Did you find something?

00:13:57.500 --> 00:14:03.040
Tomorrow at the supermarket in the next town, there’s a carrot sale—three for 50 yen.

00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:04.130
That’s cheap!

00:14:04.130 --> 00:14:05.030
I know!

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:07.440
Tomorrow, let’s have sautéed carrots over rice.

00:14:07.440 --> 00:14:08.490
Okay, Onee-chan?

00:14:08.710 --> 00:14:13.180
That’s right, sautéed carrots go pretty well with rice.

00:14:13.180 --> 00:14:14.500
And we’ll get three for only 50 yen.

00:14:26.170 --> 00:14:28.810
Asu-chan, you’ve been going home early lately.

00:14:28.810 --> 00:14:29.370
Yeah!

00:14:30.010 --> 00:14:31.330
See you later!

00:14:31.330 --> 00:14:33.310
Three carrots for 50 yen!

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:33.810
What?

00:14:35.420 --> 00:14:38.440
Ah! Three carrots for 50 yen!

00:14:42.930 --> 00:14:46.440
With the rain, it’ll be a lot harder to get to that supermarket.

00:14:50.350 --> 00:14:51.690
Ginko-chan…

00:14:52.210 --> 00:14:53.040
<i>I’m going too.</i>

00:15:01.570 --> 00:15:02.830
Ginko-chan!

00:15:03.200 --> 00:15:04.610
I won’t lose!

00:15:04.610 --> 00:15:06.550
Today, I have to buy them!

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:09.300
I will not fail!

00:15:13.870 --> 00:15:17.270
<i>Ginko-chan… just why are you trying so hard?</i>

00:15:57.380 --> 00:15:59.180
Just a little further…

00:16:01.380 --> 00:16:03.350
Yes!

00:16:03.380 --> 00:16:05.480
Man, I got here late.

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:08.610
Ah, as expected, they’re already sold out.

00:16:18.230 --> 00:16:19.740
It’s difficult, isn’t it?

00:16:20.890 --> 00:16:23.940
It really is difficult to save money, isn’t it?

00:16:23.940 --> 00:16:25.420
R-Really?

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:25.540
for 50 yen

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:25.540
1 day sale

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:25.540
3 carrots

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:27.130
Yes, very.

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:25.670
for 50 yen

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:25.670
1 day sale

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:25.670
3 carrots

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:25.790
for 50 yen

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:25.790
1 day sale

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:25.790
3 carrots

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:25.920
for 50 yen

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:25.920
1 day sale

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:25.920
3 carrots

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:31.380
1-day sale

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:31.380
3 carrots

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:31.380
for 50 yen

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:31.380
It’s even harder than working for the student council.

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:36.880
It’s over. There’s no way I can go back home.

00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:41.350
That’s not true! You just have to give your sister an honest explanation and she’ll understand.

00:16:41.350 --> 00:16:44.980
I told you! My sister is a perfectionist!

00:16:44.980 --> 00:16:48.790
Making the same mistake twice is unacceptable!{am I even bothering to consider the ages of these people when editing their speech :v}

00:16:48.790 --> 00:16:50.010
That and…

00:16:50.010 --> 00:16:51.070
And…?

00:16:54.960 --> 00:16:58.460
I’m sorry, but I must be going now.

00:16:58.460 --> 00:17:01.910
Huh? You’re not going to go talk to her?

00:17:01.910 --> 00:17:06.470
No, It wouldn’t do her any good.

00:17:09.810 --> 00:17:15.450
All I do is make mistakes and disappoint my sister.

00:17:18.420 --> 00:17:23.390
If I talk to her now, she’ll just end up feeling worse when we get home.

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:26.400
I’m sure that she hates me.

00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:31.590
She probably already hates me!

00:17:31.590 --> 00:17:33.900
You love your sister, right?

00:17:35.340 --> 00:17:38.080
It’s because you love her that you don’t want to disappoint her, right?

00:17:40.420 --> 00:17:43.410
How is that love—? {How is that love—?}

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:45.900
Then, do you hate her?

00:17:45.900 --> 00:17:48.740
I don’t hate her! No way!

00:17:49.130 --> 00:17:51.000
She is strict, but…

00:17:51.890 --> 00:17:53.960
Yeah, she does have a nice side.

00:17:55.410 --> 00:18:00.430
When I got a cold, and my mom and dad were away on business,

00:18:00.430 --> 00:18:03.440
the person who stayed beside me the whole night, holding my hand…

00:18:04.650 --> 00:18:06.430
It’ll be all right.

00:18:11.290 --> 00:18:12.820
I was so happy.

00:18:12.820 --> 00:18:15.290
<i>She does love her sister after all.</i>

00:18:15.290 --> 00:18:16.450
Let’s go home.

00:18:16.450 --> 00:18:21.860
I don’t know how to keep your sister from getting angry,

00:18:21.860 --> 00:18:23.870
but I think you should still tell her.

00:18:24.630 --> 00:18:26.700
Because you did your best.

00:18:26.700 --> 00:18:29.030
That’s all that matters. That’s it.

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:31.940
That’s right. As long as you’ve tried, that’s enough.

00:18:32.410 --> 00:18:34.340
I’m sure your sister will understand.

00:18:34.670 --> 00:18:36.950
Onee-chan?! Why are you here?

00:18:38.940 --> 00:18:40.180
I wonder why?

00:18:49.400 --> 00:18:52.460
I’m going to tell my sister the truth.

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:57.420
I’m going to tell her that I didn’t get the carrots.

00:18:58.830 --> 00:19:01.240
Because I tried my best.

00:19:02.120 --> 00:19:04.610
Yes. That sounds good.

00:19:11.420 --> 00:19:12.550
I’m home.

00:19:22.650 --> 00:19:25.530
Onee-sama, I’m sorry.

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:29.370
Yes?

00:19:29.370 --> 00:19:31.050
I couldn’t buy them.

00:19:31.050 --> 00:19:34.030
I tried my hardest, but I still didn’t get the carrots.

00:19:34.030 --> 00:19:35.370
I’m sorry.

00:19:37.800 --> 00:19:39.180
It’s okay.

00:19:40.540 --> 00:19:42.190
I know you tried your hardest.

00:19:44.860 --> 00:19:48.700
Also, I’m glad you told me the truth.

00:20:05.940 --> 00:20:07.110
Wait!

00:20:12.140 --> 00:20:15.240
It’s great that you’re back on good terms with your sister.

00:20:15.240 --> 00:20:17.820
Yes, thank you for everything.

00:20:17.820 --> 00:20:19.600
You’re welcome.

00:20:19.600 --> 00:20:22.530
Hey, we can get along too, if you want.

00:20:24.550 --> 00:20:27.450
I mean, it’s okay if we become friends.

00:20:29.860 --> 00:20:31.030
Ginko!

00:20:31.730 --> 00:20:34.510
Coming, Onee-sama!

00:20:39.720 --> 00:20:42.490
I think I can understand how Ginko-chan feels.

00:20:42.490 --> 00:20:43.390
Hmm?

00:20:43.930 --> 00:20:45.230
Little sisters…

00:20:46.010 --> 00:20:48.860
Eh? Ah, what? What about little sisters?

00:20:49.460 --> 00:20:51.630
Nothing at all! Nothing.

00:20:53.610 --> 00:20:56.800
<i>Little sisters love their big sisters.</i>

00:20:57.770 --> 00:21:02.770
<i>That’s why we’ll even tell them lies to keep them from hating us.</i>

00:21:03.720 --> 00:21:05.510
<i>No matter what type of sisterly relationship,</i>

00:21:05.510 --> 00:21:07.890
<i>even if we don’t understand each other yet,</i>

00:21:08.750 --> 00:21:13.720
<i>we still hope that we can
live a peaceful life together.</i>

